// An embedded MSR's `_restrict` formula that is wider than one line.
//
// An embedded rule prints through `rulePrinter`, which hands
// `prettyRuleRestrGen` the formula printer
// `ppRes = prettySyntacticLNFormula . toLFormula`
// (Theory/Sapic/Print.hs:41-44#rulePrinter), and the restriction item is the
// Doc composition `ppRestr' fact = operator_ "_restrict(" <> ppRestr fact <>
// operator_ ")"` (Theory/Model/Rule.hs:1382#ppRestr').  Because the formula
// is a Doc inside that composition rather than a finished string, the break
// its conjunction takes (Theory/Model/Formula.hs:493-496) indents the second
// conjunct by the ten columns of `_restrict(`.
//
// The step is reprinted in the `process=` attribute of the rule it generates,
// once modulo E and once modulo AC, so the shape appears twice.
//
// Compared slice: the `theory … end` echo.  The wf report is clean on both
// engines, so this row pins the echo alone.  No process under
// tamarin-prover/examples carries an embedded `_restrict` at all: every
// `_restrict(` there sits in a protocol rule, which a different parser reads,
// so this shape is reachable only from a fixture.

theory SapicMsrRestrictWrap
begin

functions: aaaaaaaaaa/1, bbbbbbbbbb/1, cccccccccc/1

process:
  in(<xxxxxxxxxx, yyyyyyyyyy, zzzzzzzzzz>);
  [ ] --[ Ev(xxxxxxxxxx), _restrict( aaaaaaaaaa(xxxxxxxxxx) = bbbbbbbbbb(yyyyyyyyyy) & cccccccccc(zzzzzzzzzz) = aaaaaaaaaa(yyyyyyyyyy) ) ]-> [ ];
  out('a')

end
